# Sync and slides: slides start on the first frame that shows them, reflow their siblings, settle and expire on a pinned
# clock; a node that gains a background blur stops sliding, and one that holds a blur appears in place; reduced motion;
# a script node's finished background run redraws its layer.
# frames within 1: Go repaints an edit in the bands the full paint of the view used, so it equals a full paint; Rust's
# resvg path repaints the dirty rectangle alone, where cut curves shift their antialiased edges (phase 10a).
# repaint pixels 4: with 4 cores (the hosted Windows runner) a band edge of the full paint cuts a curve, whose shifted
# antialiasing Go's banded repaints keep and Rust's dirty-rectangle repaints do not (1 pixel, 14 levels).
{"cmd":"open","path":"slides.pen"}
{"cmd":"render","w":220,"h":160,"cam":[-10,-10],"zoom":0.25,"bg":[30,30,30]}
{"cmd":"update","ids":["n1"],"props":{"enabled":true}}
{"cmd":"slide_in","id":"n1"}
{"cmd":"update","ids":["n3"],"props":{"enabled":true}}
